<title>FRANCE: Pinault-Printemps in management shake-up.</title>
<headline>Pinault-Printemps in management shake-up.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>French retailer Pinault-Printemps-Redoute said in a statement it had decided to name new heads at its main operating divisions, reporting to chairman Serge Weinberg.</p>
<p>Francois-Henri Pinault will be made managing director of the FNAC stores chain from May 5. Jean-Claude Darrouzzet will move to Conforama on May 1 and become chairman in September 30 upon retirement of Jean-Claude Tate.</p>
<p>Jean-Pierre Letranchant will be made chairman of the credit and financial services unit Finaref while Alain Viry will take the helm at the CFAO international trade unit.</p>
<p>Gilles Guinchard will become president of Rexel Inc.</p>
</text>
